fm-fleet-snapshot.sh --contribution-input live reproduction
=============================================================
Goal: reproduce the reported "Argument list too long" crash end-to-end with
the real jq binary and the real kernel ARG_MAX (getconf ARG_MAX = 2097152 on
this host), then confirm the fix on the target commit using the same FM_HOME.

Fixture: FM_HOME/data/backlog.md with 15,000 queued rows (1,563,927 bytes of
source markdown), run with `env -i PATH=/usr/bin:/bin FM_HOME=... <script>
--contribution-input`.

--- base commit b062eb94c50a68dd4467fba25346a7d7b4083288 (pre-fix) ---
$ fm-fleet-snapshot.sh --contribution-input
exit=0
stdout: 0 bytes
stderr: fm-fleet-snapshot.sh: line 1997: /usr/bin/jq: Argument list too long

Bug reproduced exactly as reported: the contribution-input branch built its
jq invocation with `--argjson backlog "$BACKLOG_JSON"`, passing the full
backlog JSON as a single argv entry. With 15k rows this exceeds ARG_MAX, the
exec of jq fails, and because the script's `exit 0` on the next line runs
unconditionally, the failure is swallowed: exit 0 with silently empty stdout.

--- target commit bae290328e90ccacc499011bb53c5a54f2e4bc8b (fix) ---
$ fm-fleet-snapshot.sh --contribution-input
exit=0
stdout: 17,126,820 bytes
stderr: (empty)
$ jq -e '(.backlog.records | length) == 15000' out.json  => true

Fixed: backlog/task JSON is now written to temp files and read back with
`--slurpfile`, so the jq argv no longer scales with backlog size. Same
FM_HOME, same 15,000-row backlog, now succeeds and emits complete, valid JSON.

--- fail-loud guard (bae2903's second fix on top of 29cdc08) ---
Fault-injected a jq wrapper that fails only on the final contribution-input
assembly call (`jq -n --slurpfile ... '{backlog:$backlog[0],tasks:$tasks[0]}'`),
small backlog, same FM_HOME for both:

commit 29cdc08 (file-transport added, no guard yet):
  exit=0, stdout 0 bytes, stderr "jq: simulated assembly failure"
  -> silently reports success despite the jq failure.

commit bae2903 (target, guard added):
  exit=1, stdout 0 bytes
  stderr:
    jq: simulated assembly failure
    fm-fleet-snapshot: contribution input assembly failed
  -> fails loudly as intended.
